# Auto-commit after each change

After finishing a discrete code change (feature, fix, or refactor), **create a git commit** using the standard commit protocol (status → diff → log → stage → commit → verify). Do not wait to be asked.

- Never push unless the user asks.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
- Prefer one commit per completed change; split unrelated pending work when practical.
- Follow the repo’s existing commit message style.
